\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0    The love that Jesus has for me
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 gives my soul much joy and peace.
\par I shall see the love that moved Him
\par to come down into this world.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par That He came as our redeemer,
\par   and to pay our price for sin.
\par Offered himself as sacrifice
\par   and died in our place instead.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.   His love for us made Him distressed
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 on top of the olive mount,
\par because of love He perspired much
\par  as blood in the garden there.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par He allowed God's wrath to come on
\par His head because of His love.
\par Because of  love, He drank a cup
\par that was very bitter too.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  Love made Him listen to insults
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj that the sinners held at Him.
\par Just for love, He gave Himself up
\par for sinners to scorned and teased;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj He wore on his head crown of thorns,
\par His head that they hit with clubs,
\par and again they spat on his face,
\par and spanked Him with strong long canes.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Just for love, he allowed his folks
\par      to pass wrong judgement on Him.
\par       And the elders committed Him
\par       into the hands of aliens.
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Those who He came as their Saviour
\par considered Him as guilty,
\par they made Him to carry his cross,
\par sent Him away from the town.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Just for love, He allowed Himself
\par       to be crucified and died.
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 The hands he came to bless us with,
\par they pierced wickedly with nails.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par The Lord of Host left Him alone,
\par as the sinful men deserves,
\par that we can witness his suff'ring
\par and the sadness of his soul.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  6. Just for love, He prayed so strongly
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj for those who ill treated Him.
\par Love to them he demonstrated
\par not to Mary his mother
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj and to John alone who heard him
\par that the robber close by him,
\par had a gracerful invitation
\par to be in his Paradise.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. The hands of Jesus which he stretched
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj across his own crucifix
\par his own statement which he made that
\par "I thirst for water to drink"
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj He revealed His love for mankind,
\par and to all the whole wide world
\par that he will hug them very well
\par as He's yearning for their souls.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. Just for love, he suffered so much;
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 love was what made him to die;
\par but He also said : "I've finished"
\par and His soul departed Him.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par This pronouncement He made tells us
\par that His love was ne'er in vain
\par whosoever gives himself up
\par will have everlasting peace.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 9\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 9.  Jesus, your love for me also
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 give my soul much joy and peace.
\par Thou has forgiven me my sins,
\par and an everlasting life.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And for this i give Thee my thanks
\par and shall forever love thee.
\par Make me just one of your servants,
\par let me be in paradise`.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

